By 4 October, ticket [#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) held **412 unique reports** about dates
showing the wrong day. Deduplicating the export by report ID and checking each tenant's
locale and booking form shows two different problems, not one.

| Problem | Reports | Evidence | Follow-up |
| --- | ---: | --- | --- |
| Shared parser reads month first for day-first locales | **379** | 11 tenants; app 204, email 150, form 25 | [Issue #1](https://github.com/MahabirSandhuHB/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1) |
| Booking-v3 date hint conflicts with day-first locale | **33** | 3 tenants; all 33 arrived through forms | [Issue #2](https://github.com/MahabirSandhuHB/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2) |

## What the reports show

The shared parser treated dates as month-first. In day-first tenants, dates entered outside
the booking-v3 form could therefore flip the day and month. These 379 reports arrived from
1 April through 4 October 2026. Intake tagged 356 as `parser` and 23 as `hint`, which
shows why the intake tag alone cannot identify the cause.

The other 33 reports came from booking-v3 forms used by day-first tenants. Those forms
instructed people to enter `MM/DD/YYYY`, while the tenant read the date day-first. The
reports came from alder.physio (12), copper.studio (11), and pale.harbour (10), from
17 April through 22 September 2026. Intake tagged 18 as `hint` and 15 as `parser`.

The export contains 427 rows because 15 report IDs appear more than once. Each report ID
is counted once above. The cause split uses the tenant locale and form behavior described
in `src/lib/kb/causes.ts`, not the intake tag.

## Engineering outcome: 5 October 2026

The engineering update on the [course challenge page](https://hq.mega.dev/challenges/what-it-shows)
reports that #4471 closed on 5 October:

| Problem | Disposition | Engineering update |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Shared parser (379 reports; Issue #1) | **FIXED** | `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales` |
| Booking-v3 date hint (33 reports; Issue #2) | **WON'T FIX** | booking-v3 form retired |

These are different outcomes: the parser was fixed, but the hint was not fixed; its form
was retired. Close Issue #1 as completed and Issue #2 as not planned. These dispositions
come from the desk's engineering update, not from a product fix implemented in this repo.

